WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.140
This is the Singularity Daily, for Wednesday, November 25.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.860
Who's driving? In four Silicon Valley towns,

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.950
Uber's new robotaxis are now testing with nobody at the wheel.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.910
Lucid has delivered over 100, and the public gets to ride early next year.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.470
Meanwhile,

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:38.920
many at Anthropic and OpenAI reportedly doubt their most powerful unreleased models can be released safely.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.150
One researcher told Axios: make them smarter than us,

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.180
and they'll be able to trick us.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.260
This week, OpenAI's chief scientist asked labs to agree on a speed limit,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.630
and how to measure it.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.950
And in Britain, Meta's assistant Muse will now do your Christmas shopping,

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.460
but it asks before it buys.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.010
Now, the money. Anthropic's shares slipped below their $83 IPO price,

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.480
just days after a record listing.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.670
Over in Taiwan, chipmaker TSMC added $158 billion in value in a day.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.310
And Singapore raised its growth forecast to about 6%, thanks to the AI boom.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:22.390
Plus,

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:28.510
OpenAI will pay local experts up to $8,000 a month to coach small businesses, free.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.610
In Warsaw,

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:36.500
scientists thought AI was hallucinating when AlphaFold predicted an impossibly knotted protein.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.510
It wasn't. They found it in gut bacteria: eight crossings,

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.920
the most complex protein knot yet.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.130
The catch? Hackers gave AI agents one sentence,

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.470
and they found a brand-new way in.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.960
And Tidal will delete 29 million AI songs. Almost none were ever played.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.640
Russia just launched a humanoid robot to the space station, to work outside it.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.940
Its operator wears a special suit, and the robot copies every move.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.700
And SoftBank bought the robot lab founded by Boston Dynamics' Marc Raibert.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.780
The cars can drive themselves now. Where we're all going is still up to us.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
